I just realized that one problem could be the Spark version used in the AMI changed from 1.1 to 1.2 (if you are using the latest scripts from Spark's master branch).

In that case you can do two things: (a) build SparkR for Spark 1.2 or (b) Use the launch scripts from Spark's 1.1 branch which should launch a cluster with Spark 1.1

Thanks
Shivaram

On Fri, Jan 30, 2015 at 11:27 AM, Shivaram Venkataraman <shivaram.v...@gmail.com> wrote:
> You'll need to look at the executor logs to see why they failed. You can do that by clicking on any executor name in the master UI (8080) and then clicking on `stderr`.
>
> My guess is its something basic like R not being installed on the worker nodes etc. as this error is happening very early.
>
> Thanks
> Shivaram
